[center][size=5][b]Shut Up Refiners[/b][/size]
Mutes all the [i]refiners[/i] in No Man's Sky.[/center]

[b]What it does[/b]
The refiners each run a loud mechanical loop while they work. This rewrites the
sound event they post so it never plays. The small refiner and the exosuit
refiner still make a noise when they run out of fuel, so you can tell.

[b]Options[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Refiners[/b] - the small, medium and large refiner you place on a planet[/]
[*][b]Refiners and Personal Refiner[/b] - those, plus the Personal Refiner in your
Exosuit inventory[/]
[/list]

[b]Compatibility[/b]
[list]
[*]Modifies the refiner entity files under
[i]MODELS/PLANETS/BIOMES/COMMON/BUILDINGS/PARTS/BUILDABLEPARTS/TECH/REFINER/ENTITIES/[/i]
and, for the [b]Refiners and Personal Refiner[/b] option, the player character
entity under [i]MODELS/COMMON/PLAYER/PLAYERCHARACTER/PLAYERCHARACTER/ENTITIES/[/i].
Nothing else[/]
[*]The player character entity is a large shared file, so a mod that rewrites
it will conflict outright[/]
[*]These files live in [i]NMSARC.Precache.pak[/i]
[*]Built for Cosmos v7.04[/]
[/list]

Built natively on Linux with my [url=https://github.com/SavageCore/AMUMSS/tree/feat/linux-support]AMUMSS Linux port[/url].

Source: [url=https://github.com/SavageCore/shutup-refiners]https://github.com/SavageCore/shutup-refiners[/url]